// Test fixture for task 6643 (leaf-scope Stage A's value-diff walk to PRD line 33).
//
// DELIBERATELY GEOMETRY-FREE. Stage A (`reify_eval::stage_a_eligible`) is pure
// Rust and calls no geometry kernel, so the guard that consumes this fixture
// must run in EVERY build profile including a stub build with neither gmsh nor
// OCCT. That is the task-6635 lesson: the Stage-A contract it established was
// carried only by `#[cfg(has_gmsh)]` e2es, which is why 6635 also had to add an
// in-crate `reify-mesh-morph` unit test. No `box(...)`, no realization, no
// kernel — just a derived `let` over two Length params.
//
// `is_wide` is the SAME shape as a compiler-synthesized `__guard_N` block/where
// guard cell (`ValueCellKind::Let` + `Type::Bool`; see
// `crates/reify-eval/src/graph.rs:599-605` and `reify-compiler/src/guards.rs`)
// but is NOT registered in `graph.structure_controlling`. That is exactly the
// discriminator the leaf-scoping change turns on, and the pairing it forms with
// the `stage_a_eligible_derived_let_guard_cell_diff_returns_false` unit test is
// the whole safety argument:
//
//   * `is_wide` (derived, not structure-controlling) → must NOT veto a tick.
//   * a `__guard_N` cell (derived, structure-controlling) → must STILL veto,
//     because Rule 2 is evaluated before the kind match.
//
// Ticking `width` 10mm → 10.5mm against `depth` 10mm flips `is_wide` from false
// to true, so the derived cell provably differs on a PURELY DIMENSIONAL edit —
// which is the mechanism the whole task is about (a derived cell is a pure
// function of its leaves, so it changes on every tick).

structure MorphDerivedLet {
    param width: Length = 10mm
    param depth: Length = 10mm

    let is_wide = width > depth
}
